# Simulation boundary

- Enemy movement is authored by the custom `PathGraph` / path-following
  runtime. Do not introduce NavMesh or move simulation state by writing a
  view transform directly.
- The domain owns path progress, targeting, collision, damage, leaks, and
  wave results. Views consume runtime snapshots/events and present them.
- Combat visuals come from the existing combat/effect event and payload path.
  Do not make a view authoritative for damage or apply damage from a particle
  callback.
- Keep gameplay movement deterministic and testable without a live scene.
  Scene objects may mirror the runtime position for presentation.
